THIRD-PARTY LICENSES — For My Privacy 0.1.0

For My Privacy has one runtime dependency, tldts ("dependencies" in package.json; `npm ls --omit=dev` lists it), which is bundled into the built extension together with its helper package tldts-core and the Public Suffix List data. Its own code is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). The extension is built with WXT and Vite, and a few very small pieces of WXT are copied into the built extension (.output/chrome-mv3). Vite's modulepreload polyfill is turned off in wxt.config.ts, so no Vite code ends up in the extension. Those pieces, and nothing else, are listed here.

How this list was made
1. Read the built files in .output/chrome-mv3 (background.js and chunks/messages-*.js, tries-*.js, lock-*.js, options-*.js, popup-*.js; the lock, options and popup chunks import the shared messages chunk, and the lock and options chunks also import the tries chunk) and matched every code fragment that is not from this repository to its source package.
2. Checked each source package's name, version, license field and license text in node_modules.
3. Checked that the build output has no other bundled library code: no import of a package name, no bundler module-wrapper helpers (__commonJS, __esm, __toESM, __defProp), no Vite helpers (modulepreload polyfill, __vitePreload), and no node_modules paths.
To check again after a dependency change: build, then search the output for those markers and re-read the minified files. Tools used only to build, test or release (TypeScript, Vitest, Playwright, Node) put no code into the extension and are not listed.

Bundled pieces

1. @wxt-dev/browser 0.3.7 (MIT) — the one-line "browser" handle (globalThis.browser if it has a runtime id, else globalThis.chrome), present in background.js and in the shared chunks/messages-*.js. Reached through "wxt/browser". Source: https://github.com/wxt-dev/wxt
2. wxt 0.21.5 (MIT) — the defineBackground helper and the small background start-up wrapper with its no-op logger. Reached through "wxt/utils/define-background". Source: https://github.com/wxt-dev/wxt
3. tldts 7.5.1 (MIT) — finds the registrable domain of a typed address (the getDomain function), bundled into the options page chunk chunks/options-*.js only (the background script, the lock page and the popup do not contain it). Source: https://github.com/remusao/tldts
4. tldts-core 7.5.1 (MIT) — the shared code of tldts. Source: https://github.com/remusao/tldts
5. Public Suffix List (MPL-2.0) — the list of public suffixes (such as co.uk and github.io) that tldts carries as data. It is unmodified data compiled into the same files as item 3. Source and license: https://publicsuffix.org/ and https://github.com/publicsuffix/list (MPL-2.0 text: https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/)

